    "created_at": "2023-10-25T10:03:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-25T10:03:27Z",
    "body": "I think this ties into cookie layering  / cookie standardization efforts and I agree with Dylan that we should standardize the apparent default behavior in browsers of allowing these requests :)\r\n\r\nThe other interesting \"breakage\" we noticed was that top-level sandboxed documents which would embed \"same-site\" resources would not send credentials as part of those requests, i.e. if you follow the above STR step 1 and set cookies on kungfoo.net arguably you should be able to load the video on https://cr2.kungfoo.net/cookies/v2/csp-page.php (using SameSite=None cookies only of course), but it's blocked by browser's third-party cookie blocking.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure whether this is really a privacy protection (it's really the same first party, it just voluntarily opts to isolate itself), but I've heard @arturjanc and @ddworken argue that it could be a security feature :)",
