    "created_at": "2023-10-25T11:07:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-25T11:07:45Z",
    "body": "My quick take on this is that it's reasonable to send cookies when previewing media resources that respond with the CSP sandbox header -- this is because an authenticated request is only sent to the exact same URL which set the header to load the previewed resource, which is safe for the hosting site.\r\n\r\nHowever, in the general case, for requests issued by sandbox documents (without the `allow-same-origin` flag) we probably don't want requests same-site with the hosting origin to carry cookies. This is because sites usually use CSP sandbox for content outside of the site's own control (e.g. HTML uploaded by the user, ads, etc.) -- we want to protect sites that do so from unwittingly re-opening themselves to cross-site attacks initiated by such sandboxed content.",
